      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for the multiple replies.  Thinking about this more, you could do the following:\n\nioex_init() unconditionally sets IOEX_FLAGS_INITIALIZED (after the IOEX_FLAGS_DISABLED check).\n\nThen ioex_init_default() skips ports that have IOEX_FLAGS_INITIALIZED set.  This then only prevents the IOEX port from getting initialized by the HOOK_INIT.  Boards would be free to call ioex_init() multiple times if warranted.\n\nI also thing it could be a good cleanup to to change IOEX_FLAGS_DISABLED to IOEX_FLAGS_DEFAULT_INIT_DISABLED.  Then move the check of IOEX_FLAGS_DEFAULT_INIT_DISABLED also into ioex_init_default().  This way, all the board code can remove the explicit clear of the IOEX_FLAGS_DISABLED.  But this is outside the scope of your change.",
